;; Reviewed 2026-10-09 by the user (written by Claude, from design
;; section 14, the LLVM backend's output, the guest runs and the debugger
;; run). Why this is right:
;; - OutBasics imports Out, rtl/vax/Out.Mod compiled with it (its .mar is
;;   expected-vax-Out.mar): its initializer calls OUT_INIT first, and its
;;   calls of Out's procedures are to their global symbols, with G^.
;; - Out.Int and Out.Hex take HUGEINTs, so each argument is widened to a
;;   quadword in the frame and passed by its address, as any HUGEINT value
;;   parameter is: -7 as ^XFFFFFFF9 and ^XFFFFFFFF, an INTEGER by CVTWL
;;   and ASHL #-31 for its high longword, a LONGINT likewise.
;; - MIN(HUGEINT) is ^X00000000 and ^X80000000, low longword first. Until
;;   2026-10-09 the voc-built poc wrote ^X7FFFFFFF for its high longword
;;   (voc's DIV is wrong for a dividend near MIN, vishap-bugs 07; HalfText
;;   now uses ASH), and its Hex printed 7FFFFFFF00000000.
;; - Out.String gets a literal's address and its length with the 0X, as
;;   any open array.
;; - Built with -build under -O2 and -OC and run on the VAX, it prints
;;   output-O2.expected and output-OC.expected, the LLVM backend's output.
; OutBasics, written by poc (doc/developer/vax-macro32-backend.md)
